            <div class="faq-container">

                <h2 class="faq-heading">FAQs</h2>

                <div class="faq-list">

                    <details class="faq-item" open>
                        <summary>How does URL shortening work?</summary>
                        <p>
                            URL shortening works by taking a long URL and
                            creating a shorter, condensed version that
                            redirects to the original URL. When a user
                            clicks on the shortened link, they are
                            redirected to the intended destination.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            Is it necessary to create an account to use the
                            URL shortening service?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            No, you can shorten URLs without creating an
                            account. However, creating an account may give
                            you access to additional features such as link
                            management and analytics.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            Are the shortened links permanent? Will they expire?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            Shortened links generally remain active unless
                            they are deleted, disabled, or subject to the
                            service's usage policies.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            Are there any limitations on the number of URLs
                            I can shorten?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            The number of URLs you can shorten depends on
                            your subscription plan and the service's usage
                            limits.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            Can I customize the shortened URLs to reflect
                            my brand or content?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            Yes, custom aliases and branded domains can
                            help you create memorable links that reflect
                            your brand or content.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            Can I track the performance of my shortened URLs?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            Yes, link analytics can provide information
                            about clicks and other engagement metrics,
                            depending on the features available on your plan.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            How secure is the URL shortening service? Are the
                            shortened links protected against spam or
                            malicious activity?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            Security measures may include suspicious-link
                            detection, abuse reporting, and restrictions on
                            malicious URLs. Always verify unfamiliar links
                            before opening them.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            What is a QR code and what can it do?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            A QR code is a scannable, two-dimensional code
                            that can direct users to a website or other
                            digital content. It can make sharing links
                            quicker and easier.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>
                            Is there an API available for integrating the
                            URL shortening service into my own applications
                            or websites?
                        </summary>
                        <p>
                            API availability depends on the service and
                            subscription plan. An API can allow developers
                            to create and manage shortened URLs from
                            their own applications.
                        </p>
                    </details>

                </div>

